<article class="env-lemma" id="00UR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00UR">Lemma <span data-tag="00UR">10.150.3</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map of finite presentation. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R \to S$ is formally étale, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R \to S$ is étale. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume that $R \to S$ is formally étale. Then $R \to S$ is smooth by Proposition <a href="/tag/00TN" data-tag="00TN">10.138.13</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00UO" data-tag="00UO">10.148.3</a> we have $\Omega _{S/R} = 0$. Hence $R \to S$ is étale by definition. 
    <p>
      Assume that $R \to S$ is étale. Then $R \to S$ is formally smooth by Proposition <a href="/tag/00TN" data-tag="00TN">10.138.13</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00UO" data-tag="00UO">10.148.3</a> it is formally unramified. Hence $R \to S$ is formally étale. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>